{"id": "t13", "value": 459, "low": 452, "high": 465, "reason": "The theory says the vote levels off a few samples past 4, once the tie block has resolved (about +5 by k = 9 in holds_against). So the vote over 9 should sit at the preliminary vote over 8 (458 in work-60f040) plus 1 or 2. The base's 33 problems with 0 of 4 right cap it below pass@4."},
{"id": "t14", "value": 199, "low": 191, "high": 207, "reason": "Under the theory, 8 samples gain only the base's tie problems over the vote over 4 (192, result-5c961a). The near-zero block caps votes on hard sets: the base has no right sample on 26 of RL's 36 wins and 100 problems unsolved (knowledge-dab63f), so the gain is a few problems."},
